{
  "title": "62: al-Jomoa'h الجمعة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيُسَبِّحُ لِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ الْمَلِكِ الْقُدُّوْسِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَكِيْمِ‏(1)\nYOSABBEHO LILLAAHE MAA FIS SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZIL MALEKIL QUDDOOSIL A’ZEEZIL HAKEEM.\nWhatever there is in the heavens and in the earth glorifies Allah, the Sovereign, the All-holy, the All-mighty, the All-wise.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ بَعَثَ فِى الْاُمِّيّٖنَ رَسُوْلًا مِّنْهُمْ يَتْلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ وَيُزَكِّيْهِمْ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَاِنْ كَانُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ لَفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(2)\nHOWAL LAZEE BA-A’SA FIL UMMIYYEENA RASOOLAM MINHUM YATLOO A’LAYHIM AAYAATEHI WA YOZAKKEEHIM WA YO-A’LLEMOHOMUL KETAABA WAL HIKMATA, WA IN KAANOO MIN QABLO LAFEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nIt is He who sent to the unlettered [people] an apostle from among themselves, to recite to them His signs, to purify them, and to teach them the Book and wisdom, and earlier they had indeed been in manifest error.\nوَّاٰخَرِيْنَ مِنْهُمْ لَمَّا يَلْحَقُوْا بِهِمْ‌ؕ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(3)\nWA AAKHAREENA MINHUM LAMMAA YALHAQOO BEHIM, WA HOWAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nAnd to others from among them [as well] who have not yet joined them. And He is the All-mighty, the All-wise.\nذٰ لِكَ فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ يُؤْتِيْهِ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(4)\nZAALEKA FAZLUL LAAHE YOA-TEEHE MANY YASHAAA-O, WAL LAAHO ZUL FAZLIL A’ZEEM.\nThat is Allah’s grace, which He grants to whomever He wishes, and Allah is dispenser of a great grace.\nمَثَلُ الَّذِيْنَ حُمِّلُوا التَّوْرٰٮةَ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَحْمِلُوْهَا كَمَثَلِ الْحِمَارِ يَحْمِلُ اَسْفَارًا‌ ؕ بِئْسَ مَثَلُ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(5)\nMASALUL LAZEENA HUMMELUT TAWRAATA SUMMA LAM YAHMELOOHAA KAMASALIL HEMAARE YAHMELO ASFAARAA, BEA-SA MASALUL QAWMIL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE AAYAATIL LAAH, WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nThe example of those who were charged with the Torah, then failed to carry it, is that of an ass carrying books. Evil is the example of the people who deny Allah’s signs, and Allah does not guide the wrongdoing lot.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْۤا اِنْ زَعَمْتُمْ اَنَّكُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ لِلّٰهِ مِنْ دُوْنِ النَّاسِ فَتَمَنَّوُا الْمَوْتَ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(6)\nQUL YAA-AYYOHAL LAZEENA HAADOO IN ZA-A’MTUM ANNAKUM ANNAKUM AWLEYAAA-O LILLAAHE MIN DOONIN NAASE FATAMANNAWUL MAWTA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nSay, ‘O Jews! If you claim that you are Allah’s favourites, to the exclusion of other people, then long for death, should you be truthful.’\nوَلَا يَتَمَنَّوْنَهٗۤ اَبَدًۢا بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(7)\nWA LAA YATAMANNAW-NAHU ABADAM BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEHIM, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUM BIZ-ZAALEMEEN.\nYet they will never long for it, because of what their hands have sent ahead, and Allah knows best the wrongdoers.\nقُلْ اِنَّ الْمَوْتَ الَّذِىْ تَفِرُّوْنَ مِنْهُ فَاِنَّهٗ مُلٰقِيْكُمْ‌ ثُمَّ تُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰى عٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(8)\nQUL INNAL MAWTAL LAZEE TAFIRROONA MINHO FA-INNAHU MOLAAQEEKUM SUMMA TORADDOONA ELAA A’ALEMIL GHAYBE WASH-SHAHAADATE FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nSay, ‘The death that you flee will indeed encounter you. Then you will be returned to the Knower of the sensible and the Unseen, and He will inform you about what you used to do.’\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا نُوْدِىَ لِلصَّلٰوةِ مِنْ يَّوْمِ الْجُمُعَةِ فَاسْعَوْا اِلٰى ذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ وَذَرُوا الْبَيْعَ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(9)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA NOODEYA LIS SALAATE MINY YAWMIL JOMO-A’TE FAS-A’W ELAA ZIKRIL LAAHE WA ZARUL BAY’, ZAALEKUM KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nO you who have faith! When the call is made for prayer on Friday, hurry toward the remembrance of Allah, and leave all business. That is better for you, should you know.\nفَاِذَا قُضِيَتِ الصَّلٰوةُ فَانْتَشِرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَابْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِ اللّٰهِ وَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ كَثِيْرًا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(10)\nFA-EZAA QOZEYATIS SALAATO FANTASHEROO FIL ARZE WABTAGHOO MIN FAZLIL LAAHE WAZKORUL LAAHA KASEERAL LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nAnd when the prayer is finished disperse through the land and seek Allah’s grace, and remember Allah much so that you may be felicitous.\nوَاِذَا رَاَوْا تِجَارَةً اَوْ لَهْوَا۟ اۨنْفَضُّوْۤا اِلَيْهَا وَتَرَكُوْكَ قَآئِمًا‌ ؕ قُلْ مَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ مِّنَ اللَّهْوِ وَمِنَ التِّجَارَةِ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَيْرُ الرّٰزِقِيْنَ‏(11)\nWA EZAA RA-AW TEJAARATAN AW LAHWAA NINFAZZOO ELAYHAA WA TARAKOOKA QAAA-EMAA, QUL MAA I’NDAL LAAHE KHAYRUM MENAL LAHWE WA MENAT TEJAARAH, WAL LAAHO KHAYRUR RAAZEQEEN.\nWhen they sight a deal or a diversion, they scatter off towards it and leave you standing! Say, ‘What is with Allah is better than diversion and dealing, and Allah is the best of providers.’",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Madani’ Surah and it has 11 ayaat. Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if this Surah is recited frequently in the mornings and evenings, the reciter is protected from the influence of Shaitan and his temptations. His sins are also forgiven.\nIn another narration it is said that if a person recites this Surah daily, he will be safe from every dangerous and frightening thing."
}
